## Final Judgement
### Summary of Key Insights
The retrieved evidence shows that Kristen Welker did not personally make financial donations to Barack Obama, Hillary Clinton, or Joe Biden. Instead, these political contributions—amounting to tens of thousands of dollars—were made by her parents, Julie and Harvey Welker. Furthermore, while Welker was registered as a Democrat in Rhode Island in 2004 and Washington, D.C. in 2012, her current registration status is not specified. Lastly, Welker and her family did attend a Christmas event at the White House with the Obamas in 2012. Because the evidence clearly addresses the core aspects of the claim, no further investigation is required.

### Conclusion
Based on the fact-check, the decision is `refuted`. The assertion that Kristen Welker personally gave thousands of dollars to Obama, Clinton, and Biden is false, as official records attribute these donations to her parents rather than Welker herself. While some elements of the claim contain elements of truth (such as her past Democratic registration and attending a White House Christmas event), the central accusation of personal financial bias through political donations is explicitly contradicted by the evidence.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted because there is no record of NBC News journalist Kristen Welker personally making financial donations to Barack Obama, Hillary Clinton, or Joe Biden. According to a report by the [New York Post](https://nypost.com/2020/10/17/kristen-welker-next-debate-moderator-has-deep-democrat-ties/), these political contributions—including nearly $20,000 to Obama, $2,100 to Clinton, and $3,300 to Biden—were actually made by her parents, Julie and Harvey Welker. While Welker was previously registered as a Democrat in Rhode Island in 2004 and Washington, D.C. in 2012, her current registration status is unspecified. Additionally, although she and her family did attend a Christmas event at the White House with the Obamas in 2012, the central accusation of her personal financial bias through political donations is false.